# Vendored dependencies -- the Makefile clones/downloads all of these fresh
# on first build (see the ifeq($(wildcard ...)) blocks near its top), so
# committing them here would just be an untracked-drift-prone copy of
# someone else's upstream repo.
/lvgl
/dr_libs
/tinyalsa
/faad2
/alac
/mbedtls
/cJSON
/dbus
/opus
/lua

# Stock-firmware UI assets (theme2 PNGs). Proprietary HiBy graphics --
# never redistributed, see README.md's own note on this. Populate this
# locally from your own device/firmware dump if you want to build with the
# real UI; assets/fonts/ (this repo's own, openly-licensed subsets, see its
# own NOTICE.md) is tracked normally.
#
# A handful of files under here are exceptions, confirmed NOT present in a
# genuine stock firmware dump (diffed directly against one) -- this app's
# own boot animation and Subsonic integration icons, not HiBy IP, so they're
# safe to track normally. Excluding everything else in the tree first, then
# re-including just those specific paths one directory level at a time --
# git won't apply a file-level negation inside a directory that's still
# itself excluded, so each level needs its own `!` before the next. Anyone
# who populates the rest of this directory locally from their own firmware
# dump (per the note above) won't have those real stock files
# accidentally un-ignored by this.
/assets/theme2/*
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/
/assets/theme2/boot_animation/*
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/
/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/*
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/0.png
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/config.ini
!/assets/theme2/boot_animation/en/push.bat
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/
/assets/theme2/stream_media/*
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/subsonic.png
!/assets/theme2/stream_media/subsonic_s.png

# Korean.ttf-derived host-simulator font: excluded, unlike the rest of
# assets/fonts/, because this particular file's own embedded metadata
# doesn't state a license (see assets/fonts/NOTICE.md). Populate locally
# from your own device dump (/usr/resource/fonts/Korean.ttf, subsetted to
# U+1100-11FF,U+3130-318F,U+AC00-D7A3) if you want Korean text to render in
# `make host`'s simulator -- on target this is a non-issue, the real device
# build reads Korean.ttf directly from the stock firmware at runtime.
/assets/fonts/korean.ttf

# Build outputs
/build_host/
/build_target/
/open_hiby_player_host
/open_hiby_player_target
/open_hiby_player_target_*
/compile_commands.json
/compile_flags.txt

# Host-only runtime state (target uses /usr/data instead)
/open_hiby_player_settings.txt*
/open_hiby_player_peq.txt*
/open_hiby_player_music.db

# Host-only test audio fixtures (generated locally for manual verification,
# not needed to build or run the project)
/music/

# Local Python helper scripts, including files created in any future
# subdirectory. Tracked Python files remain tracked by Git as usual.
*.py

# Local GUI-refactor extraction workspace
/scratch/

# Local-only known-issues tracker (not part of the public docs)
/ISSUES.md

# Claude Code
/CLAUDE.md
.claude/
